<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūtrĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient town in Etruria</i>, now <i>Sutri</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 6, 3, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
			14</span></i>. — Prov.: quasi eant Sutrium, i. e. <i>to set about any thing well prepared</i> (as
			Camillus, when he marched to the conquest of Sutrium), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas.
				3, 1, 10</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 310</span></i> Müll.
			— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūtrīnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Sutrium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 8, § 51</span></i>
			. — <i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūtrīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Sutrium</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 6,
			3</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sūtrĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Sutrium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tecta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 493</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
